rota lap 5133, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; the happy zone and the thin edge. digest_record_read is pure decision in the happy zone, and the record's five readings are its contract; leg 28 is the contract check that presses each field alone. The flow tasted off at exactly the seam where a proof had been written rather than run.
think The round-open parked stash@{0} at 203145, one minute before this lap opened, and its base was bd61c9df38 -- HEAD exactly. So this replay was not a merge, and I applied it whole.
think The paper it carried read Status Landed and claimed 30 legs GREEN. I ran the control before believing that sentence, which is the water row's own instruction.
think First run RED: the build left no remembered record naming the compiler. The binary on this pier was built from an elder source carrying the SAME rye_version, so the control's staleness door read stands at or past its source and waved through a binary that behaved differently. Moved rye_version to this lap's stamp and said in the doc comment beside it that a behavior change in that file moves that stamp.
think Second run, against a candidate built from the true source, RED again: a record whose path disagreed with the file was trusted. digest_record_read computed seen_path and never read it -- four of the five identity readings refused a record and the fifth did not exist.
think So the paper's own sentence about six deletions planted one at a time cannot have been true, and it was the ledger's row rather than a typo: a proof written rather than run reads exactly like a proof.
think Repaired with one line and its reason, rebuilt, control GREEN at 30 legs on metal. Booked %781 off the spine's --next, and the send's rebase found a peer had published it -- so the view moved to %784 and the stamp 20260916.204153 never did, which is rule 4 doing its ordinary work.
obs The plant that proves the new line bites is history rather than a fresh mutation -- the comparison was absent and leg 28 reddened. Saying that plainly is cheaper and truer than re-deleting a line I just watched fail.
obs Held still through the cold roster pass rather than rebuilding rye/bin/rye under it; FileBusy was the pier telling the truth. Built to rye/bin/rye.cand and handed the control that path, which it takes as its first argument for exactly this.
